From 84b91753d41c2466deeb16489f5bc1617bdb2588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:00:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/36] The studio's decisions, as pure modules

Three disclosure levels, one capability descriptor that says per field whether
a knob can be turned and which of the three possible reasons refuses it, the
curated samplers over the runtime's own vocabulary, family working points with
their reason, training buckets, the pass chain, the LoRA stack, client-side
wildcards, A1111 weighting, seed batching and the X/Y/Z matrix.

No Dexie, no components, no IPC: every one of these is a function of its
arguments, which is what lets the panel above them be tested by reading text
off a rendered page instead of by generating pictures.
